    "body": "## Problem\n\nA delivered harness task can remain in progress in its canonical backlog. Updating it after final review would also leave the status commit outside the reviewed candidate.\n\n## What changes\n\nAdd durable backlog closeout between unit acceptance and final review. The coordinator commits Done status, passing evidence and an honest compare reference in the implementation branch, then renews exact-commit unit checks and obtains separate final acceptance. Rejection or source changes require committed cleanup of stale status and evidence before work resumes.\n\nApply that rule to FOS-000026 and correct FOS-000025 against its merged PR #2 and retained historical verification. Split tasks use tracked canonical definitions so merging the implementation PR also updates their backlog entries.\n\n## Why this matters\n\nContributors and future agents can use the canonical backlog without a separate closeout change. Interrupted, failed or unsupported required work cannot be presented as completed.\n\n## Why this approach\n\nThe existing Git checkpoint helper records intent, prepared bookkeeping and cleanup obligations. A restricted metadata edit preserves requirements and dependencies, and checker-only renewal covers the extra commit without consuming a repair attempt. This adds one review pass while preserving the one-PR workflow.\n\n## Verification and limits\n\nAll 34 Python/Git harness tests passed, including real source commits, rejection cleanup, accepted schema-2 adoption, split requirements preservation and local publication/recovery scenarios. Skill metadata validation passed. An original-helper counterexample reproduced publication with a Pending backlog. Independent unit and final reviews cover the committed implementation and backlog update.\n\nHistorical FOS-000025 evidence is attributed to its original revision. No C++/Vulkan, GPU, Steam or hosted CI claims follow from these checks. Deterministic publication tests are separate from this PR's live publication.\n\n## Task references\n\n- [FOS-000026: include backlog completion in the implementation PR](https://github.com/robinwassen/Fossilize/blob/codex/FOS-000026-backlog-completion/local-docs/reviews/harness-backlog.md#fos-000026--include-backlog-completion-in-the-implementation-pr)\n- [FOS-000025: historical completion reconciled against merged PR #2](https://github.com/robinwassen/Fossilize/pull/2)\n",
